Problem definition:

Incompressible Euler equations.
Viscous and Inviscid flow: rho_ref, vel_ref, temp_ref, p_ref
are set to 1.0 in order to perform a dimensional calculation.
Force coefficients computed using initial values.
The reference area for force coeffs. is 0.341011 m^2.
The reference length for force coeffs. is 0.284176 m.
The pressure is decomposed into thermodynamic and dynamic components.
The initial value of the dynamic pressure is 0.
Mach number: 0.0528684, computed using the Bulk modulus.
For external flows, the initial state is imposed at the far-field.
Angle of attack (deg): 2, computed using the initial velocity.
Side slip angle (deg): 0, computed using the initial velocity.
SI units only. The grid should be dimensional (meters).
No energy equation.
-- Input conditions:
Fluid Model: CONSTANT_DENSITY 
Thermodynamic pressure not required.
Bulk modulus: 142000 Pa.
Initial dynamic pressure: 0 Pa.
Initial total pressure: 198.45 Pa.
Initial density: 1.225 kg/m^3.
Free-stream velocity: (17.989, 0, 0.628191) m/s. Magnitude: 18 m/s.
